  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Educate 850 Mainly Muslim Girls out of Poverty</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Girls in the Old City of Hyderabad, India, face challenges in getting a proper education which would help them break out of poverty.   The MJM school, which serves them, was once a top tier school but has fallen on hard times as its funding, infrastructure and teaching quality have declined. Enrollment which at its peak was 2500 has fallen to 450. Girls have to walk 4-6 kms to a government school  The project would modernize curriculum, improve teaching and take girls to financial independence.</narrative>
  </description>
